# 03 - Multiple Button Iputs

## Objective
Create a program using an ESP32 where pressing each button lights  the corresponding LED up, and when both buttons are pressed, both LEDs light up.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- LED
- 220 Ω resistor
- Push button
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- GPIO Output
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- INPUT_PULLUP
- digitalWrite()
- if/else statements
- variables

## Wiring

- LED Anode → GPIO 16
- LED Cathode → GND (through a 220 Ω resistor)
- Push button pin 1 → GPIO23
- Push button pin 2 → GND

## Expected Result

When the button is pressed, the LED turns on and stays on after releasing the button, then when the button is pressed again, the LED turns off and stays off after releasing the button.

## What I Learned

- What Input pullups are and how to use them
- How to properly if/else statements

## Resources

- ESP32 Documentation
- Arduino Documentation
